      "identification": "Device-code phishing landing page with a French shared-document pretext; matches a publicly reported relay architecture without proving a particular kit or operator.",
      "execution_trace": [
        "Page-load async function POSTs to /api/device/start using a fixed X-Antibot-Token header.",
        "Returned user_code is displayed and copied on the copy-button click; the verification button opens the legitimate Microsoft device-login site.",
        "A five-second timer polls /api/device/status/<encoded session_id>; completed status stops the timer and replaces the page with /document."
      ],
      "verdict_basis": "The document pretext, separate Microsoft device authorization, gated backend relay and session-completion redirect together support deceptive account authorization. Microsoft reports this backend/header architecture in device-code phishing.",
      "limitations": [
        "Backend implementation, OAuth client ID/scopes, token destination and actual victim authorization are absent. Do not claim that this frontend acquires or exfiltrates OAuth tokens itself."
      ],
      "sources": [
