    {
      "identification": "SharpShares .NET x64 share auditing utility; behavior matches mitchmoser/SharpShares public source. Exact release hash provenance is unverified.",
      "execution_trace": [
        "Resolved the CLR entrypoint and decoded IL for all 34 methods using dnfile/dncil; resolved generic method targets and enumerated native imports and resources.",
        "Main parses caller arguments, collects LDAP/OU computer DNS names, deduplicates hosts, starts progress reporting and invokes bounded parallel share enumeration.",
        "NetShareEnum level 1 returns share records. GetComputerShares filters share names, uses Directory.GetFiles to check read access, and compares filesystem ACLs against the current user/group SIDs to report write access.",
        "Output goes to Console or the user-selected outfile via a locked File.AppendText routine. The write-access result is inferred from ACLs; no remote write probe is performed.",
        "All managed calls, P/Invokes and resource entries were reviewed. No added payload, credential capture, persistence, arbitrary execution, or external collector was found."
      ],
      "verdict_basis": "Observed behavior matches a publicly available administration/assessment tool and its advertised CLI. Offensive deployment is possible, but no delivery chain, unauthorized use or added malicious behavior is supplied.",
      "limitations": [
        "The file is unsigned and lacks a verified release hash. The CI-style PDB path supports a rebuild, not an authenticated publisher.",
        "The reproducible-build marker means timestamp fields may be content-derived values; they are not reliable build dates.",
        "Do not infer benign intent from the absence of a detection; the verdict rests on complete IL-path review and comparison with public implementation."
      ],
