    {
      "identification": "HypeAgent-style Windows abuse source fragment; the supplied C is not a complete executable RAT.",
      "execution_trace": [
        "enable_hidden_rdp calls set_service_dll for TermService and UmRdpService; the helper opens HKLM service Parameters with KEY_SET_VALUE and writes ServiceDll to ProgramData wrapper DLL paths.",
        "disable_hidden_rdp restores the ordinary system DLL paths. No DLL dropping, service stop/start, or actual in-memory patch routine is present; patch names are an unused string array.",
        "install_mitm_root_ca passes the handle from CertOpenSystemStoreA(0, ROOT) directly to CertAddEncodedCertificateToStore; this modifies the current-user store, not the machine store.",
        "format_mitm_proxy_status only formats JSON. Claims that WinINet/HKLM proxies are enabled, QUIC is disabled and traffic is intercepted are status strings, not implemented operations.",
        "The session routine formats caller-supplied ChatGPT, Claude and Cursor cookies into headers and sends HTTPS GET requests to real account endpoints using WinHTTP. Response data is read into a local buffer and discarded; it neither acquires cookies nor meaningfully classifies session validity."
      ],
      "verdict_basis": "Deliberate hidden-RDP service redirection and a stolen-session replay workflow together support a malware-oriented source fragment. Solar 4RAYS independently describes the same paired wrapper paths, patch vocabulary and AI account-endpoint checks in HypeAgent. These corroborate mechanism and context, not this exact source-file hash.",
      "limitations": [
        "No main/entrypoint, dispatcher, wrapper DLL bodies, root certificate bytes, credential acquisition, collector, configured C2 or deployment context is included.",
        "The absent DLLs prevent proving hidden-session operation. A diagnostic proxy can legitimately install a root, and API clients can legitimately check cookies, so the generalizable traits retain only two suspicious findings and neutral capability observations.",
        "Do not import unrelated HypeAgent capabilities from the external report into this sample."
      ],
      "sources": [
